WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.360
Live support provides situational awareness without taking command from the pilot.

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:08.215
The center may track mission status, crew check-ins, weather, airspace changes,

00:00:08.215 --> 00:00:12.715
telemetry summaries, communications, data milestones, and outstanding hazards.

00:00:12.715 --> 00:00:16.940
Status boards should show what requires action: mission phase, crew, aircraft, location,

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:21.345
communication state, battery or timing milestones, warnings, and escalation status.

00:00:21.345 --> 00:00:25.215
Stale data must be marked clearly rather than presented as current.

00:00:25.215 --> 00:00:26.360
Communication discipline matters.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:30.190
Safety-critical messages receive priority, standard terms reduce ambiguity,

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:33.105
and the center avoids flooding the pilot with nonessential requests.

00:00:33.105 --> 00:00:37.415
Payload or client questions wait when aircraft control requires attention.

00:00:37.415 --> 00:00:41.800
Emergency support can provide contacts, maps, weather, airspace information, coordination,

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:42.800
and a decision log.

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:46.420
The center should know when to contact emergency, aviation, site, security,

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:49.080
or management authorities under approved procedures.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:52.868
Abort criteria belong to the plan and are monitored during the mission.

00:00:52.868 --> 00:00:56.120
Weather, aircraft warnings, battery anomalies, signal degradation,

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:58.420
people entering the area, privacy concerns,

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:01.398
or loss of authorization may require return or landing.

00:01:01.398 --> 00:01:04.960
Handoffs preserve authority and context when shifts or teams change.

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:09.420
After landing, an after-action review captures deviations, decisions, equipment issues,

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:10.960
data quality, and lessons.

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:14.810
Live support adds value when it reduces pilot workload and improves organizational

00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:15.405
learning.

00:01:15.405 --> 00:01:18.440
When several missions are active, the center must prioritize attention.

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:21.210
High-risk phases, emergency calls, lost communication,

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:25.360
and deteriorating conditions take precedence over routine status updates.

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:27.520
Staffing and displays should reflect that hierarchy.
